Spec: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/spec.md (Ordering, Parser seam, Logs, Store at runtime; AC20, AC25, AC29, AC59)
Research: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/research.md Q10, Q11 (db_deleted relies on the inode check; db_read_only on open handles still writing inline rows)
Why this approach: pipeline.go is the plan's five steps in one worker call, with Release deferred. A parser panic is recovered in the worker and logged once through logging.LogPanic as the capture_failed line (type and stack, never the value). A Canonicalize error or an unknown status becomes parse failed. The parse reasons are fixed strings so no body data reaches a log. The decode cap reaches ParseInput through a new capture.Config.DecodeLimit. Recorded in plan.md ("Details fixed in T14").
Alternatives rejected: carrying max_body_bytes on core.Exchange (it would change core for a worker-only need); logging the parser's or Canonicalize's error text (it can quote body bytes); skipping SaveParse for a nil parser (the row would keep parse NULL instead of skipped).
Trade-off / known limit: db_read_only makes the store directory read-only after startup, since open SQLite handles can't be made read-only from outside; what fails is the blob write for an over-4-KiB body (the Q11 behaviour). A request body is joined twice per exchange (SaveExchange and ParseInput). An exchange whose SaveParse fails keeps its raw row with parse NULL.
Verified by: make verify; go test -race -count=3 ./internal/capture ./internal/core. New tests: TestStore_ConcurrentWorkersNoBusyErrors (8 workers, 500 exchanges, parse skipped on each), TestCapture_StoreDeadClientUnaffected (db_deleted/deleted_logged_once, db_read_only, write_fails), TestCapture_ParsePanicIsFailed, TestCore_TestParserNeedsNoCoreChange, TestRedact_AdapterQueryParams/in_store; they first failed to build on the missing DecodeLimit. Mutations, each reverted: dropping the store-failure log failed all three StoreDead subtests; removing the recover failed ParsePanicIsFailed; Canonicalize with nil exclusions failed TestParserNeedsNoCoreChange; skipping SaveParse failed ConcurrentWorkers, ParsePanic and TestParserNeedsNoCoreChange; storing the unredacted query failed in_store.
